    "28": {
      "date": "2026-10-05",
      "edition": "Monday 5 October",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Coaching search",
          "heading": "Warren Gatland among 31 applicants to become new Fiji head coach",
          "body": "Former Wales boss Warren Gatland has emerged as a surprise candidate to lead Fiji, following reports that 31 coaches have applied to succeed Mick Byrne. The recruitment process enters its final stage today, coinciding with the official start date listed in the original job advertisement. While interim coach Senirusi Seruvakula currently oversees the squad, the Fiji Rugby Union is expected to name a permanent appointment shortly to lead the Flying Fijians against France, Ireland and Italy next month."
        }
      ],
      "match": {
        "venue": "Groupama Stadium, Lyon"
      },
      "source": {
        "name": "Planet Rugby"
      }
    },
    "386": {
      "date": "2026-10-05",
      "edition": "Monday 5 October",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Coaching identity",
          "heading": "Steve Borthwick retains RFU backing despite persistent scrutiny over England’s tactical identity",
          "body": "Steve Borthwick retains the long-term backing of the RFU to lead England into next year’s World Cup, despite ongoing scrutiny regarding the team’s tactical direction. While the head coach is praised for a 'Spock-like approach' to analysis, critics suggest his tenure is marked by contradictions between data-led pragmatism and the team's best performances when playing with more freedom. Following a review-heavy period and a historic loss to Italy, Borthwick must now reconcile his reputation for 'thinking like a machine' with the need for a settled, cohesive gameplan."
        }
      ],
      "source": {
        "name": "Guardian Rugby Union"
      }
    },
    "387": {
      "date": "2026-10-05",
      "edition": "Monday 5 October",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "World Ranking",
          "heading": "France maintained the world number one ranking for one week",
          "body": "France held the top spot in the official world rankings for a single week between July 2022 and July 2022. This remains the longest unbroken spell at No. 1 in the world for the nation."
        }
      ],
      "rung": "data"
    },
    "388": {
      "date": "2026-10-05",
      "edition": "Monday 5 October",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Coaching history",
          "heading": "Peter O’Mahony details his disappointment over Rassie Erasmus’s Munster departure",
          "body": "Former captain Peter O’Mahony has revealed the impact of Rassie Erasmus’s departure from Munster, admitting the exit left him feeling hurt at the time. Speaking on the Indo Sport podcast, the veteran forward explained that he had fully committed to the director of rugby’s game plan and believed the team was on the cusp of significant progress. While acknowledging that it was a ruthless business decision, O’Mahony noted he now understands the professional motivation behind the move back to South Africa."
        }
      ],
      "source": {
        "name": "SA Rugby Magazine"
      }
    },
    "389": {
      "date": "2026-10-05",
      "edition": "Monday 5 October",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Statistical review",
          "heading": "Italy men’s XV record across the last 11 international matches",
          "body": "Italy have navigated a demanding period of international rugby, conceding 318 points across their last 11 outings. The side has registered 190 points in that same window, averaging 17.3 points scored and 28.9 points conceded per match. Their most successful result in this recent sequence remains the 34-19 home victory over Chile, achieved during the November 2025 international window."
        }
      ],
      "rung": "data"
    },
    "390": {
      "date": "2026-10-05",
      "edition": "Monday 5 October",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Selection prospect",
          "heading": "Hector Patterson monitors options as Bath circle Edinburgh scrum-half prospect",
          "body": "Edinburgh scrum-half Hector Patterson is attracting interest from English and French clubs, with Bath reportedly tracking the 21-year-old. Patterson, the son of former Scotland international Derrick, remains under contract at Edinburgh but his eligibility for England via a grandparent presents an intriguing subplot. Having represented Scotland through the age-grade system, including a win at the 2024 World Rugby U20 Trophy, his international future remains open until he is senior-capped. His next move is being closely watched ahead of the 2027 Rugby World Cup."
        }
      ],
      "source": {
        "name": "Guardian Rugby Union"
      },
      "rung": "storyline"
    },
    "391": {
      "date": "2026-10-05",
      "edition": "Monday 5 October",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "URC form",
          "heading": "Cardiff and Dragons shine as regional hopefuls push for Wales spots",
          "body": "Cardiff and Dragons have emerged as the early pacesetters in the United Rugby Championship, securing unbeaten starts to the campaign. While international regulars continue to impress abroad, the domestic form of these two sides is drawing attention to potential squad bolters. Dragons head coach Filo Tiatia praised his group’s resilience following their six-try derby victory, noting, \"You are not just fighting for the players on the field. There is a deeper understanding in the group around what they are actually fighting for.\""
        }
      ],
      "source": {
        "name": "BBC Rugby Union"
      }
    },
    "460": {
      "date": "2026-10-05",
      "edition": "Monday 5 October",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Statistical review",
          "heading": "Argentina maintain high scoring output across their recent international campaign",
          "body": "Argentina have shown a potent but porous form in their recent outings, recording a total of 321 points scored across their last 11 international matches. While the attacking displays have been consistent, Los Pumas have also conceded 346 points during that same period. These totals result in an average of 29.2 points scored and 31.5 points conceded per game. Their most productive performance in this 11-match window remains the 52-28 victory secured away against Wales in November 2025."
        }
      ],
      "rung": "data"
    },
    "461": {
      "date": "2026-10-05",
      "edition": "Monday 5 October",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "World Cup ambitions",
          "heading": "Jeremy Williams backs resurgent Wallabies to challenge for 2027 World Cup",
          "body": "Wallabies lock Jeremy Williams has backed Australia to challenge for the Webb Ellis Cup at next year’s home World Cup, as the team continues to build momentum under coach Les Kiss. Currently ranked sixth in the world, the side has remained unbeaten under Kiss, whose tenure has seen a first series win in Argentina and a gritty victory against South Africa. \"The team we’ve got, the players, coaching staff, and the drive, the care that we have for each other,\" Williams said."
        }
      ],
      "source": {
        "name": "Guardian Rugby Union"
      }
    },
    "463": {
      "date": "2026-10-05",
      "edition": "Monday 5 October",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Match history",
          "heading": "Japan prepare to face Wales following narrow defeat last November",
          "body": "As Japan continue their international programme, they look towards their next outing against Wales. The two sides last met in November 2025 during an international friendly fixture. On that occasion, Japan suffered a narrow 24-23 defeat away from home. The team currently holds a record of one win and two losses from their 3 matches played, leaving them 10th on the log with a points difference of -26."
        }
      ],
      "rung": "data"
    },
    "465": {
      "date": "2026-10-05",
      "edition": "Monday 5 October",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Tactical approach",
          "heading": "Dave Rennie confirms All Blacks remain committed to aerial game tactics",
          "body": "All Blacks head coach Dave Rennie has confirmed the side will not abandon their high-ball strategy, despite difficulties encountered against the Springboks during the recent Rugby's Greatest Rivalry series. New Zealand has adopted a tactic of sprinting back to catch kicks rather than running onto the ball. Rennie acknowledged the team struggled aerially against South Africa but maintained they are moving in the right direction, noting that the players have embraced the high-tempo style he is instilling since taking charge."
        }
      ],
      "source": {
        "name": "Planet Rugby"
      }
    },
    "467": {
      "date": "2026-10-05",
      "edition": "Monday 5 October",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Coaching vacancy",
          "heading": "Jake White emerges as favourite for Fiji head coach role",
          "body": "Former Springboks head coach Jake White has reportedly emerged as the leading candidate to take charge of Fiji ahead of the 2027 Rugby World Cup. While Fiji’s national union has received 31 applications for the vacancy, sources indicate White is currently the favourite to be appointed. If successful, it would mark White’s first international head coaching role since leading South Africa to World Cup glory in 2007. The appointment is expected to be confirmed in the coming days."
        }
      ],
      "source": {
        "name": "Planet Rugby"
      }
    }
